    "introduction": "International Airlines Group brings together airlines including British Airways, Iberia, Aer Lingus and Vueling. Its businesses carry passengers and cargo across short-haul and long-haul networks, supported by loyalty and other travel-related activities. Revenue comes from tickets, ancillary services and freight, with fares and capacity managed across routes and seasons. Different airline brands serve different customer segments and geographic strengths. The business requires significant spending on aircraft, maintenance, staff and airport access, while fuel is a major operating input. Performance depends on travel demand, seat utilisation and pricing, alongside reliable operations and the ability to manage disruption across complex flight networks.",
